{
  "format": "evn-blocks",
  "version": 2,
  "title": "ADC: every block",
  "needs": "the ADC module on I2C port 1, and voltages of 0 to 3.3 V on A0..A3 (for example a potentiometer between the board's 3.3 V and GND pins, its middle pin on A0); never more than 3.3 V on a pin",
  "description": "The voltage on all four inputs, A0 to A3, twice a second for 10 s. An input with nothing wired to it floats: it reads a wandering few tenths of a volt, not 0.",
  "workspace": {
    "blocks": {
      "languageVersion": 0,
